Ground Beef Stir Fry
  --Gina Matsoukas

Sauce:
3 tbsp coconut aminos, substitute tamari/shoyu
1 tsp minced garlic
1 tsp minced fresh ginger
1 tsp sriracha
1 tsp rice vinegar
1 tbsp toasted sesame oil
1 1/2 tbsp maple syrup
2 tbsp water
1 tbsp arrowroot powder, substitute tapioca starch or cornstarch

Whisk together all the ingredients for the stir fry sauce in a small bowl and set aside.

Stir Fry:
1 lb ground beef
1 tbsp evoo
1 red bell pepper, chopped
1 large carrot, cut into matchsticks
1/2 lb asparagus, ends trimmed, chopped
8 oz mushrooms, sliced or quartered
1/2 a large yellow onion, chopped
sesame seeds, for garnish
sliced scallions, for garnish

Place a large skillet over medium-high heat. Once hot, add the ground beef and cook until browned. Transfer to a plate and set aside. Add the olive oil to the pan and let it get hot. Once hot, add the prepared vegetables and sauté for about 5 minutes until starting to soften but still slightly crisp. Add the beef back to the skillet and toss to combine with the vegetables. Pour in the stir fry sauce, stir immediately to coat all the ingredients and turn off the heat. The sauce should thicken quickly. Garnish with sesame seeds and scallions and serve with cooked white rice.


Notes: I cook onions first, add beef after. Also made with tofu instead, works. Added chili crisp, would recommend low sodium shoyu if using that. Can use any veggies you want, can use ground chicken, turkey, etc.
